    body: '- Quotation — issued by the seller, stating the price, quality and quantity offered\n- Order — issued by the buyer, requesting supply of specified goods\n- Proforma invoice — issued by the seller before the order is confirmed, for customs and foreign exchange\n- Invoice — issued by the seller after supply, showing the amount owed by the buyer\n- Receipt — issued by the seller, confirming that payment has been received\n- Credit note — issued by the seller to reduce the amount owed; a debit note increases it\n- Lorry note — issued for goods sent by road, signed by the consignee on delivery\n- Consignment note — issued by the carrier for goods taken in, used for rail consignments\n- Air waybill — issued for air cargo; a receipt and contract of carriage, not a document of title\n- Bill of lading — issued by the sea carrier: receipt, contract of carriage and document of title\n- Warehouse receipt — issued by the warehousekeeper for goods deposited; a document of title\n- Dock warrant — issued by a dock warehouse; a document of title allowing goods to be taken up\n- Certificate of origin — states where goods were produced, attested by a chamber of commerce\n- Certificate of inspection — states that goods were examined and meet the required standards\n- Letter of credit — issued by a bank, assuring the exporter of payment against documents\n- Draft (bill of exchange) — an unconditional written order to pay, used in foreign trade\n- Policy schedule — issued by the insurer, listing the perils covered and the premium payable'
